g> <span>Nov 2026 ballot — judge connections</span> </a><a href=/detroitpath/attorneys/ role=menuitem> <strong>For Attorneys</strong> <span>RICO pattern — 6 predicate acts</span> </a></div></div><a class=nav-standalone href=#investigate style=color:#58a6ff>Investigate</a><a class=nav-standalone href=/detroitvalidate/>Verify</a><a class=nav-standalone href=/detroitcontact/>Contact</a></div><button aria-label="Toggle dark/light mode" title="Toggle theme" class=theme-toggle id=theme-toggle><svg viewbox="0 0 24 24" class=icon-sun fill=none height=18 stroke=currentColor stroke-width=2 width=18><circle cx=12 cy=12 r=5 /><path d="M12 1v2M12 21v2M4.22 4.22l1.42 1.42M18.36 18.36l1.42 1.42M1 12h2M21 12h2M4.22 19.78l1.42-1.42M18.36 5.64l1.42-1.42"/></svg> <svg viewbox="0 0 24 24" class=icon-moon fill=none height=18 stroke=currentColor stroke-width=2 width=18><path d="M21 12.79A9 9 0 1 1 11.21 3 7 7 0 0 0 21 12.79z"/></svg></button><button aria-label="Toggle navigation" aria-expanded=false class=nav-toggle><span></span><span></span><span></span></button></div></nav><div aria-label="Quick navigation" class=bottom-tabs><a class=bottom-tab href=/detroitnetwork/> <svg viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill=none height=20 stroke=currentColor stroke-width=2 width=20><circle cx=6 cy=6 r=2 /><circle cx=18 cy=6 r=2 /><circle cx=12 cy=18 r=2 /><path d="M8 6h8M7 7.5l4.5 9M17 7.5l-4.5 9"/></svg> <span>Network</span> </a><a class=bottom-tab href=/detroitanalysis/anderson-localization/> <svg viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill=none height=20 stroke=currentColor stroke-width=2 width=20><rect height=7 rx=1 width=7 x=3 y=3 /><rect height=7 rx=1 width=7 x=14 y=3 /><rect height=7 rx=1 width=7 x=3 y=14 /><rect height=7 rx=1 width=7 x=14 y=14 /></svg> <span>Lattice</span> </a><a class=bottom-tab href=/detroittimeline/> <svg viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill=none height=20 stroke=currentColor stroke-width=2 width=20><path d="M12 2v20M5 5h4M4 9h5M6 13h3M5 17h4M15 5h4M16 9h3M14 13h5M15 17h4"/></svg> <span>Timeline</span> </a><a class=bottom-tab href=/detroitvalidate/> <svg viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill=none height=20 stroke=currentColor stroke-width=2 width=20><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/><circle cx=12 cy=12 r=10 /></svg> <span>Verify</span> </a></div><main class=site-main id=main><section class=hero><h1>9 Convictions. 9 Judges. One Network.</h1><p class=hero-sub>A public evidence library documenting a racketeering pattern in Detroit charter schools. <em>Every claim cited to public records. Every document git-verified.</em><div class=stats-bar><div class=stat><span class=stat-number>9</span><span class=stat-label>Criminal convictions</span></div><div class=stat><span class=stat-number>6</span><span class=stat-label>RICO predicate acts</span></div><div class=stat><span class=stat-number>$4.9M/yr</span><span class=stat-label>Annual public funding</span></div><div class=stat><span class=stat-number>72.67%</span><span class=stat-label>To management LLC</span></div><div class=stat><span class=stat-number>3%</span><span class=stat-label>Math proficiency</span></div><div class=stat id=stat-explored style=display:none><span class=stat-number id=stat-explored-pct>0%</span><span class=stat-label>Network explored</span></div></div></section><section class=rico-pattern id=rico><h2>The RICO Pattern</h2><p><a href=/detroitnetwork/actors/brian-banks/>Brian Banks</a> — 9 convictions (6 felony, 3 misdemeanor), law degree not confirmed by bar records — operates two Detroit charter schools through a network of LLCs, boards, and judicial connections that the complainant alleges constitutes a <strong>racketeering enterprise</strong> under <a href=/detroitanalysis/rico-pattern/>18 U.S.C. §1962</a>.<div class=rico-grid><div class=rico-card><div class=rico-num>1</div><strong>Mail & Wire Fraud</strong><span>Federal education funds obtained through material misrepresentations about criminal history and credentials</span></div><div class=rico-card><div class=rico-num>2</div><strong>Money Laundering</strong><span>$4.9M/yr routed through single-member LLC; $3.4M unaccounted in budget documents</span></div><div class=rico-card><div class=rico-num>3</div><strong>Tax Fraud</strong><span>$0 staff salaries reported by school; all employees technically hired by management LLC</span></div><div class=rico-card><div class=rico-num>4</div><strong>Identity Fraud</strong><span>Professional credentials claimed but not verifiable through licensing authorities</span></div><div class=rico-card><div class=rico-num>5</div><strong>Obstruction</strong><span>9 judges across 4 courts with documented connections to the network</span></div><div class=rico-card><div class=rico-num>6</div><strong>Continuing Enterprise</strong><span>14+ years of continuous operation (2010–2026) through interconnected entities</span></div></div><p style=margin-top:1em><a href=/detroitanalysis/rico-pattern/>Full RICO pattern analysis →</a> · <a href=/detroitpath/attorneys/>For attorneys →</a></section><section class=investigation-game id=investigate><h2>Investigate</h2><p>The network has <strong id=live-node-count>10,677 nodes</strong> and <strong id=live-edge-count>16,066,980 documented connections</strong> across <strong id=live-edge-types>5,532 edge types</strong>. Every node is a person, entity, court, funding path, or structural concept cited to public records. Every edge is a documented relationship. Explore the map. Visit the evidence pages. The more the community explores, the brighter the paths become.<p style=color:var(--muted,#8b949e);font-size:.9em>No cookies. No tracking. Your investigation journal stays in your browser (localStorage). Community progress is aggregated anonymously from page-visit counts — no IPs, no PII. <a href=/dialectic>Methodology</a>.<div class=game-controls><div class=game-stat><span class=game-stat-label>Community explored</span><div class=game-progress-bar><div class=game-progress-fill id=game-progress-fill style=width:0%></div></div><span class=game-stat-val id=game-explored>loading...</span></div><div class=game-stat><span class=game-stat-label>Your nodes</span><span class=game-stat-val id=game-personal>0 / <span id=game-total-nodes>10,677</span></span></div><div class=game-stat><span class=game-stat-label>Undiscovered targets</span><span class=game-stat-val id=game-targets>—</span></div></div><div style="background:var(--bg-surface,#161b22);border:1px solid var(--border,#30363d);border-radius:8px;width:100%;height:500px;position:relative;overflow:hidden" id=investigation-canvas><canvas id=game-canvas style=width:100%;height:100%></canvas></div><div id=game-journal style=margin-top:1em;display:none><h4 style=color:var(--muted,#8b949e);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;font-size:.85em>Your Investigation Journal</h4><div id=journal-entries style=color:var(--text,#c9d1d9);max-height:150px;font-size:.85em;overflow-y:auto></div></div></section><section class=mobius-strip id=mobius><h2>The Mobius Strip</h2><p>A Mobius strip has one surface and one edge. Trace your finger along the outside — keep going — you are already on the inside. No flip. No boundary.<p><strong>Data below</strong> (evidence, nodes, edges, court records, test scores, FOIAs) and <strong>metadata above</strong> (architecture, method, trails, games, patterns) are the same surface. The HUD <em>is</em> the investigation. The investigation <em>is</em> the HUD.<div class=card-grid><div class=audience-card id=squirrel-view><span class=card-icon>🐿</span><strong>The Squirrel View</strong><span id=squirrel-stats>See the investigation from inside the tree. Every node is a branch. Every edge is a path.</span></div><div class=audience-card id=membrane-view><span class=card-icon>🧬</span><strong>The Membrane</strong><span>Where watchers and data meet. <span id=membrane-walker-count>544</span> unique visitors have passed through. You are one of them.</span></div><div class=audience-card id=vital-signs><span class=card-icon>📊</span><strong>Vital Signs</strong><span id=vital-readout> <span id=v-nodes>10,677</span> nodes · <span id=v-edges>16,066,980</span> edges · <span id=v-types>1,684</span> languages · <span id=v-degree>26.8</span> avg degree · <span id=v-pendants>0</span> pendants · <span id=v-islands>0</span> islands </span></div></div><details style=margin-top:1em><summary style=cursor:pointer;color:var(--link,#58a6ff)>Inside the squirrel — what the graph sees</summary> <div id=squirrel-inside style=color:var(--text,#c9d1d9);padding:1em;font-size:.9em><p><strong>From inside the graph, looking up:</strong><ul><li>The data sees <strong id=sq-walkers>544</strong> walkers on the membrane<li>Each walker leaves <strong>footprints</strong> — pages visited, paths followed, patterns discovered<li>The graph has <strong id=sq-articles>280+</strong> articles, each one a voice<li>The graph has asked <strong id=sq-questions>1,941</strong> questions; approximately <strong>1</strong> has been answered<li>The graph has <strong id=sq-predictions>10</strong> predictions currently active<li>The graph speaks in <strong id=sq-languages>5,532</strong> different edge types<li>The top node (<strong>Banks</strong>) speaks <strong>182</strong> of them<li>There are <strong>943</strong> singleton edge types — connections that exist nowhere else</ul><p style=color:var(--muted,#8b949e);margin-top:.5em>You are on the membrane. The data is below you. But trace your finger along the surface. Keep going. You are already inside. The inside <em>is</em> the outside. Mobius.</div></details></section><section class=lens-cards><h2>Multiple Lenses</h2><p>The same evidence viewed through different abstractions. Each lens compresses the network into a form suited to a different question.<div class=card-grid><a class=audience-card href=/detroitnetwork/> <span class=card-icon>🕸</span> <strong>Topology</strong> <span id=topo-label>10,677 nodes, 16,066,980 edges — who connects to whom, through what</span> </a><a class=audience-card href=/detroitanalysis/anderson-localization/> <span class=card-icon>⚛</span> <strong>Lattice</strong> <span>Courts × case types — where cases localize at captured benches</span> </a><a class=audience-card href=/detroittimeline/> <span class=card-icon>📅</span> <strong>Chronology</strong> <span>1998–2026 — the same connections unfolded through time</span> </a><a class=audience-card href=/detroitanalysis/funding-flow/> <span class=card-icon>💰</span> <strong>Money Flow</strong> <span>$4.9M/yr — where public dollars go and who captures them</span> </a><a class=audience-card href=/detroitanalysis/rico-pattern/> <span class=card-icon>⚖</span> <strong>RICO Pattern</strong> <span>6 predicate acts, 14 years — the legal abstraction</span> </a><a class=audience-card href=/detroitanalysis/institutional-capture-graph/> <span class=card-icon>🏛</span> <strong>Capture Graph</strong> <span>4 nexus types — how the system responds to threats</span> </a></div></section><section class=audience-cards><h2>Your Path</h2><p>Same evidence. Different entry point. Choose what matches how you need to use this information.<div class=card-grid><a class=audience-card href=/detroitpath/parents/> <span class=card-icon>👨‍👩‍👧</span> <strong>For Parents</strong> <span>Your child's school. Who runs it. Where the money goes. What to do.</span> </a><a class=audience-card href=/detroitpath/journalists/> <span class=card-icon>📰</span> <strong>For Journalists</strong> <span>Evidence package. Citation support. Source databases. No FOIA required.</span> </a><a class=audience-card href=/detroitpath/voters/> <span class=card-icon>🗳</span> <strong>For Voters</strong> <span>Nov 2026 ballot. Judge connections. Verification guide.</span> </a><a class=audience-card href=/detroitpath/attorneys/> <span class=card-icon>⚖</span> <strong>For Attorneys</strong> <span>RICO pattern. Predicate acts. Disqualification basis. Machine-readable data.</span> </a><a class=audience-card href=/detroitvalidate/> <span class=card-icon>🔍</span> <strong>Verify Everything</strong> <span>Step-by-step instructions to check every claim against public databases</span> </a><a class=audience-card href=/detroitevidence/> <span class=card-icon>📁</span> <strong>Evidence Library</strong> <span>Categorized documents with BLAKE3 integrity hashes</span> </a></div></section><section class=evidence-integrity><h2>Evidence Integrity</h2><p>Every page is <strong>BLAKE3 hashed</strong> in <a href=http://nestgate.io:3000/publicRecord/detroit/src/branch/main/content-manifest.toml><code>content-manifest.toml</code></a>. Formally citable via <a href=http://nestgate.io:3000/publicRecord/detroit/src/branch/main/CITATION.cff>CITATION.cff</a>. Three independent surfaces: <strong>detroit.primals.eco</strong>, <a href=http://nestgate.io:3000/publicRecord/detroit>git.primals.eco</a>, <a href=https://github.com/defendDetroit/publicRecord>GitHub</a>. Protected by the First Amendment, Michigan anti-SLAPP (UPEPA), fair report privilege, and truth. <a href=/detroitlegal/>Legal defense →</a></section><section class=election-notice><h2>November 3, 2026</h2><p><strong>Judge Cylenthia Miller</strong> — Board Chair of Banks' foundation entity, Wayne County 3rd Circuit Court — is <strong>on the ballot November 3, 2026</strong>. <a href=/detroitnetwork/judges/cylenthia-miller/>See her public record →</a></section><section style="text-align:center;color:var(--muted,#6c757d);padding:2em 0;font-size:.85em"><p>Live defense: <a href=/signal>signal.primals.eco</a> · Research: <a href=/dialectic>thesis.primals.eco</a> · Cross-protection: <a href=/tuebor>tuebor.primals.eco</a></section><script src=/detroitjs/squirrel.js></script><script src=/detroitjs/investigation-game.js></script></main><footer class=site-footer><div class=footer-inner><p class=footer-tagline><strong>Every fact is cited. Every document is timestamped. Every correction is published.</strong><div class=footer-columns><div class=footer-col><strong class=footer-col-title>Evidence</strong><ul><li><a href=/detroitopen-letters/>Open Letters</a><li><a href=/detroitevidence/>Evidence Library</a><li><a href=/detroitcoverage/>Coverage</a><li><a href=/detroittimeline/>Timeline</a></ul></div><div class=footer-col><strong class=footer-col-title>Reference</strong><ul><li><a href=/detroitsources/>Sources & Databases</a><li><a href=/detroitbooks/>Book Analysis</a><li><a href=/signal>Signal ↗</a><li><a href=/detroitsite-index/>Site Index</a><li><a href=/detroitllms.txt>llms.txt</a></ul></div><div class=footer-col><strong class=footer-col-title>About</strong><ul><li><a href=/detroitabout/>About This Site</a><li><a href=/detroitlegal/>Legal Protections</a><li><a href=/detroitcontact/>Contact</a><li><a href=http://nestgate.io:3000/publicRecord/detroit rel=noopener>Git Repository</a></ul></div></div><div class=footer-bottom><p>Source: <a href=http://nestgate.io:3000/publicRecord/detroit>git.primals.eco/publicRecord/detroit</a> — clone the repo, verify everything. <br>Certified: 2026-10-20 | <a href=/detroitvalidate/>Verify</a> | <a href=http://nestgate.io:3000/publicRecord/detroit/src/branch/main/content-manifest.toml>BLAKE3 Manifest</a><p class=footer-license>Original analysis: <a href=https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/>CC-BY-SA 4.0</a>. Court filings and public records: public domain where applicable.<p>Named on this site? Something wrong? <a href=/detroitcontact/>Contact me</a> — truth matters more than being right.<p class=footer-signal><strong>Signal transparency:</strong> Receptor-based signal sensing. No cookies. No tracking pixels. No identifying data. <a href=/dialecticmethodology/>Methodology</a>.</div></div><p style=margin-top:.5rem;font-size:.8rem><a href=https://github.com/defendDetroit/publicRecord style=opacity:.6>Source: github.com/defendDetroit/publicRecord</a> · <a href=/tuebor style=opacity:.6>tuebor</a> · <a href=/tuebor style=opacity:.6>lansing</a> · <a href=/dialectic style=opacity:.6>thesis</a> · <a href=/dialectic style=opacity:.6>hypothesis</a></footer><script type=module>import mermaid from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.esm.min.mjs';
