    </script><body><a class=skip-link href=#main>Skip to content</a><nav class=site-nav><div class=nav-inner><a class=nav-brand href=/tuebor>tuebor</a><div class=nav-links><a href=/tuebor style=color:khaki;font-weight:700>🔍 Explore</a><a href=/tueboractors/>Actors</a><a href=/tueborevidence/>Evidence</a><a href=/tueboranalysis/>Analysis</a><a href=/tueborinvestigate/>Investigate</a><a href=/tuebortimeline/>Timeline</a><a href=/tueborsynthesis/ style=color:#98fb98>Dialectic</a><a href=/tuebor-desk style=opacity:.7;font-size:.85em>⊞ Desk</a><a href=/tuebormembrane/ style=opacity:.7;font-size:.85em>⬡ Membrane</a><a href=/map style=opacity:.7;font-size:.85em>🗺️ Map</a></div><div class=nav-search><input aria-label="Search articles" placeholder="Search Beasley, Moran, PCA..." autocomplete=off id=tuebor-search><div class=search-results id=tuebor-search-results style=display:none></div></div></div></nav><main class=site-main id=main><article class=page-content><h1>How To Build an OS — Dykema Gossett and the Dark Money Machine</h1><time class=page-date>October 9, 2026</time><h2 id=what-is-an-operating-system>What Is An Operating System?</h2><p>In computing, an operating system mediates between hardware and applications. It allocates resources, manages processes, and controls access. A healthy OS distributes resources to producers. A parasitic OS extracts resources for intermediaries.<p>This study maps a parasitic operating system in Michigan politics using entirely public records. The model organism is Dykema Gossett PLLC — a national law firm that doesn’t just provide legal services to dark money nonprofits. It creates them, staffs them, and operates them.<p>Every claim below can be verified from the public sources cited.<hr><h2 id=the-kernel-w-alan-wilk>The Kernel: W. Alan Wilk</h2><p>Every OS has a kernel — the privileged code that controls everything.<p>W. Alan Wilk is a Member at Dykema Gossett and Team Leader of its Political Compliance, Elections & Campaign Finance practice. He is admitted to the Michigan bar (1995), educated at James Madison College (MSU) and Boston College Law.<p>He incorporates dark money nonprofits. He files their state paperwork. He serves as their lawyer. He manages their compliance. He is also a member of the <a href=https://www.deadlinedetroit.com/articles/28989/duggan-tied_dark_money_groups_push_four_detroit_city_council_candidates rel=external>National Republican Lawyers Association</a> — and simultaneously the lawyer for the <a href=https://www.deadlinedetroit.com/articles/28819/the_messy_intersection_of_dark_money_and_detroit_politics rel=external>Democratic mayor’s campaign</a>.<p>When asked for comment by Deadline Detroit, Wilk said: <strong>“I’m not authorized to speak to the press on this.”</strong><p>The kernel doesn’t speak to userspace.<p><strong>Source:</strong> <a href=https://www.dykema.com/people/w-alan-wilk.html rel=external>dykema.com</a> · <a href=https://www.deadlinedetroit.com/articles/28989/duggan-tied_dark_money_groups_push_four_detroit_city_council_candidates rel=external>Deadline Detroit</a><hr><h2 id=the-scheduler-renae-moore>The Scheduler: Renae Moore</h2><p>A scheduler decides which processes run. Renae Moore is Dykema’s Senior Compliance Specialist (rmoore@dykema.com, 517-374-9121). She holds simultaneous roles across six entities:<table><thead><tr><th>Entity<th>Her Role<th>Entity Function<tbody><tr><td>Save Detroit Jobs / Detroit Leaders<td>Asst Secretary<td>Defeated community benefits ordinance; defeated journalist; elected council member<tr><td>Our Neighborhoods First<td>Compliance Officer<td>Promoted Duggan’s Prop N; ran attack ads against Duggan’s opponent<tr><td>Detroit Jobs First<td>Compliance Officer<td>Defeated community benefits ordinance (Prop A)<tr><td>RFFW LLC<td>Treasurer<td>Passed $1,000,000 from one donor to abortion rights ballot campaign<tr><td>Turn Around Wayne County PAC<td>Record Keeper<td>Funneled corporate money to other dark money vehicles<tr><td>Duggan Campaign<td>Compliance Officer<td>Managed compliance for the mayor’s campaign</table><p>One person. One Dykema paycheck. Six dark money operations.<p><strong>Source:</strong> <a href=https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/813772058 rel=external>IRS 990EZ</a> (EIN 81-3772058) · <a href=https://www.michigan.gov/sos/-/media/Project/Websites/sos/CFR-Complaints/2023/Meyers-v-RFFW-2.pdf rel=external>MI SOS complaint</a> (Meyers v RFFW) · <a href=https://www.deadlinedetroit.com/articles/28819/the_messy_intersection_of_dark_money_and_detroit_politics rel=external>Deadline Detroit</a><hr><h2 id=the-process-table-entities-as-spawned-processes>The Process Table: Entities as Spawned Processes</h2><p>An OS spawns processes — they look independent but share the same kernel and scheduler.<table><thead><tr><th>Entity<th>Created<th>Status<th>Function<tbody><tr><td>Save Detroit Jobs → Detroit Leaders<td>2016<td>Active (renamed twice)<td>Defeated community benefits; defeated investigative journalist; elected Latisha Johnson<tr><td>Our Neighborhoods First<td>Jul 2020<td>Active<td>Promoted Duggan’s $250M bond; attacked Duggan’s opponent<tr><td>Detroit Jobs First<td>2016<td>Active<td>Defeated community benefits (Prop A)<tr><td>RFFW LLC<td>Jul 2022<td>Dissolved<td>Passed $1,000,000 hidden donation; forced to disclose after complaint</table><p><strong>The process lifecycle:</strong><ol><li><strong>spawn</strong> — Wilk files paperwork, Moore assigned compliance<li><strong>execute</strong> — entity spends money, sends mailers, runs ads<li><strong>rename</strong> — if exposed, change name (Save Detroit Jobs → Impact Detroit → Detroit Leaders)<li><strong>dissolve</strong> — if complaint filed, dissolve entity (RFFW)<li><strong>respawn</strong> — new entity, same officers, same function</ol><p><strong>Source:</strong> LARA entity search · IRS 990 filings · Michigan SOS campaign finance · <a href=https://www.deadlinedetroit.com/articles/28930/benson-tied_non-profit_pivots_to_fighting_elrick_in_detroit_district_4_council_race rel=external>Deadline Detroit</a><hr><h2 id=the-phone-number-test>The Phone Number Test</h2><p>The simplest proof that SDJ is not independent:<p>The phone number on Save Detroit Jobs’ <a href=https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/813772058 rel=external>IRS 990EZ filing</a> (EIN 81-3772058) is <strong>517-374-9100</strong>.<p>That is <a href=https://www.dykema.com/offices/lansing.html rel=external>Dykema Gossett’s Lansing office phone number</a>.<p>If you call Save Detroit Jobs, you reach Dykema’s receptionist.<p>The entity’s tax return was prepared by <strong>Olivia RC A Flower</strong> at <strong>Dykema Gossett PLLC, 2723 S State St Ste 400, Ann Arbor MI 48104</strong> — Dykema’s Ann Arbor office.<p>SDJ doesn’t have its own phone. Doesn’t have its own office. Doesn’t prepare its own taxes. Its compliance officers are Dykema employees. Its incorporation was filed by a Dykema attorney.<p><strong>SDJ is not a nonprofit that uses Dykema. SDJ is a Dykema process wearing a 501(c)(4) costume.</strong><p><strong>Source:</strong> IRS Form 990EZ (filed Nov 11, 2024) via <a href=https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/813772058 rel=external>ProPublica Nonprofit Explorer</a><hr><h2 id=the-filesystem-domains-by-proxy>The Filesystem: Domains By Proxy</h2><p>The dark money websites hide their ownership behind <a href=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domains_by_Proxy rel=external>Domains By Proxy</a>, a GoDaddy subsidiary whose tagline is: <strong>“Your identity is nobody’s business but ours.”</strong><table><thead><tr><th>Entity Website<th>Hidden By<tbody><tr><td>ourneighborhoodsfirst.com<td>Domains By Proxy<tr><td>detroitjobsfirst.com<td>Domains By Proxy<tr><td>SDJ / Detroit Leaders<td>No website — lists Dykema’s phone</table><p>Individual privacy is a right. Entity privacy, when the entity spends $100,000+ on elections, is an accountability problem.<p><strong>Source:</strong> WHOIS records · <a href=https://www.deadlinedetroit.com/articles/26311/dark_money_flows_into_duggan_s_250_million_detroit_bond_campaign rel=external>Deadline Detroit</a> (Charlie LeDuff) · <a href=https://www.metrotimes.com/news/exclusive-former-duggan-liaison-heads-dark-money-fund-opposing-detroit-community-benefits-ordinance-2468328/ rel=external>Metro Times</a><hr><h2 id=both-parties-served>Both Parties Served</h2><p>Dykema Gossett State PAC total expenditures (2017-present): <strong> $725,000+ </strong><table><thead><tr><th>Recipient<th>Amount<th>Party<tbody><tr><td>House Republican Campaign Committee<td>$62,000<td>R<tr><td>Senate Republican Campaign Committee<td>$58,750<td>R<tr><td>Michigan House Democratic Fund<td>$45,000<td>D<tr><td>Michigan Senate Democratic Fund<td>$44,000<td>D<tr><td>Duggan Campaign<td>$13,500<td>D<tr><td>Tom Barrett for Congress (Federal PAC)<td>$4,000<td>R</table><p>The kernel is apolitical. The kernel serves whoever has root access.<p><strong>Source:</strong> <a href="https://www.transparencyusa.org/mi/committee/dykema-gossett-state-pac-505912-ind?cycle=2017-to-now" rel=external>TransparencyUSA</a> (Dykema Gossett State PAC, all cycles)<hr><h2 id=what-it-costs-detroit>What It Costs Detroit</h2><h3 id=schools>Schools</h3><p><a href=/network/entities/purpose-charter-academy/>Purpose Charter Academy</a> students score <a href=https://clutchjustice.com/2026/09/13/macdowell-preparatory-academy-academic-financial-record/ rel=external> 3% proficient in math</a>. The school’s management company takes 72.67% of revenue. The dark money vehicle that defended this arrangement — by defeating the journalist investigating it — was incorporated by Dykema, staffed by Dykema, and uses Dykema’s phone number.<h3 id=democracy>Democracy</h3><p>SDJ spent $84,000 to defeat ML Elrick — a Fox 2 investigative reporter who had exposed double-dipping taxpayer salaries by Councilman Benson’s staff. In his place: Latisha Johnson, who now sits on the Purpose Charter Academy board.<h3 id=community-self-determination>Community Self-Determination</h3><p>Two Dykema dark money vehicles combined to defeat Proposal A — a grassroots community benefits ordinance that would have required developer concessions. Combined spending: $100,000+. Funded by corporations and developers — the entities that would have been regulated.<hr><h2 id=how-to-verify>How To Verify</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Claim<th>Public Source<tbody><tr><td>SDJ phone = Dykema phone<td><a href=https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/813772058 rel=external>ProPublica Nonprofit Explorer</a><tr><td>Moore = Dykema employee<td><a href=https://www.dykema.com/people/ rel=external>dykema.com staff listing</a><tr><td>Domains By Proxy usage<td>WHOIS lookup on ourneighborhoodsfirst.com<tr><td>Dykema PAC → both parties<td><a href="https://www.transparencyusa.org/mi/committee/dykema-gossett-state-pac-505912-ind?cycle=2017-to-now" rel=external>TransparencyUSA</a><tr><td>PCA → 3% math<td><a href=https://clutchjustice.com/2026/09/13/macdowell-preparatory-academy-academic-financial-record/ rel=external>Clutch Justice</a><tr><td>LARA entities<td><a href=https://mibusinessregistry.lara.state.mi.us rel=external>MI Business Registry</a><tr><td>RFFW complaint<td><a href=https://www.michigan.gov/sos/-/media/Project/Websites/sos/CFR-Complaints/2023/Meyers-v-RFFW-2.pdf rel=external>michigan.gov/sos</a></table><p>All data is from public records about public entities performing public functions. No private information is used. This is entity accountability, not personal exposure.<hr><h2 id=this-is-a-living-document>This Is A Living Document</h2><p>This study is continuously updated as new public filings emerge. The Dykema OS is not static — entities are spawned, renamed, dissolved, and respawned. The process table changes. The analysis follows.<p><strong>Related pages:</strong><ul><li><a href=/analysis/corporate-network-lara/>The Corporate Network — LARA Entity Analysis</a><li><a href=/network/actors/>Enterprise Principals</a><li><a href=/evidence/>Evidence Library</a></ul><hr><p><em>An entity is not an individual. Public records about public entities are not private information. This is how you read a process table.</em></article><nav aria-label="Related articles" class=cross-links><h2>🔗 Connections</h2><p class=cross-desc>Other articles that touch the same entities and patterns.<div data-keywords="Dykema Gossett dark money, W Alan Wilk political compliance, Renae Moore Save Detroit Jobs, Detroit Leaders dark money, Our Neighborhoods First Duggan, RFFW LLC money laundering, Domains By Proxy dark money, Save Detroit Jobs Dykema phone number, Purpose Charter Academy dark money, bipartisan dark money Michigan, parasitic operating system, dark money infrastructure Michigan" id=cross-link-list></div><div style="background:#0d111799;border:1px solid #5ab87a33;border-radius:6px;margin-top:16px;padding:12px"><button onclick="if(window._networkFold){window._networkFold.show()}else{var s=document.createElement('script');s.src='/sensesjs/network-fold.js?v=1';s.onload=function(){window._networkFold&&window._networkFold.show()};document.head.appendChild(s)}" style="color:#58a6ff;cursor:pointer;background:#58a6ff1f;border:1px solid #58a6ff4d;border-radius:4px;padding:6px 14px;font:11px monospace" id=show-fold-btn>🧬 Open Network Fold — see who is behind the face entities</button><span style="color:#8b949e;margin-left:8px;font:9px monospace">253 nodes · 972 edges · 24 tuebor overlap</span></div></nav><section aria-label="Share what you know" class=opsonize id=opsonize><div class=opsn-header><h2>🔬 Share What You Know</h2><p class=opsn-subtitle>Every observation strengthens the network. Tag what you see, share what you know, build immunity together.</div><div class=opsn-channels><div class="opsn-channel opsn-signal"><div class=opsn-channel-header><span class=opsn-icon>📡</span><h3>Signal</h3><span class=opsn-badge>Private</span></div><p class=opsn-desc>Submit observations directly to the network. Reviewed before publication. Your IP is hashed, never stored raw.<form autocomplete=off class=opsn-form id=opsn-form><input name=page type=hidden value=/analysis/how-to-build-an-os/><div class=opsn-field><label for=opsn-tag>What type of observation?</label><select id=opsn-tag name=tag required><option value>Select a tag…<option value=witness>🔍 Witness — I have direct knowledge<option value=document>📄 Document — I have supporting documents<option value=connection>🔗 Connection — I know additional links<option value=correction>✏️ Correction — Something needs fixing<option value=confirmation>✅ Confirmation — I can confirm these facts<option value=threat>⚠️ Threat — I face ongoing harm<option value=pattern>🗺️ Pattern — I see this elsewhere<option value=resource>🤝 Resource — I can offer assistance</select></div><div class=opsn-field><label for=opsn-body>Your observation</label><textarea placeholder="What do you know? Be specific — names, dates, documents, case numbers." id=opsn-body maxlength=2000 minlength=10 name=body required rows=4></textarea><span class=opsn-hint>Min 10 characters. No personal data stored without consent.</span></div><div class=opsn-field><label for=opsn-contact>Contact (optional, encrypted)</label><input placeholder="ProtonMail, Signal number, or leave blank" id=opsn-contact maxlength=200 name=contact><span class=opsn-hint>Only used if we need to verify. Never published.</span></div><button class=opsn-submit id=opsn-submit><span class=opsn-submit-text>Send Signal</span> <span class=opsn-submit-sending style=display:none>Sending…</span></button><div class=opsn-result id=opsn-result style=display:none></div></form></div><div class="opsn-channel opsn-discuss"><div class=opsn-channel-header><span class=opsn-icon>💬</span><h3>Discuss</h3><span class="opsn-badge opsn-badge-public">Public</span></div><p class=opsn-desc>Open discussion on the membrane. Comments live on sovereign infrastructure.<div id=discuss-container></div><noscript><p class=opsn-noscript>Discussion requires JavaScript. You can also <a href=https://github.com/amicusContra/tuebor/discussions>view discussions on GitHub</a>.</p></noscript><p class=opsn-tip style=margin-top:8px><a href=https://github.com/amicusContra/tuebor/discussions rel=noopener style=color:#484f58;font-size:.85em target=_blank>↗ also on GitHub Discussions</a></div><div class="opsn-channel opsn-email"><div class=opsn-channel-header><span class=opsn-icon>🔐</span><h3>Secure Message</h3><span class="opsn-badge opsn-badge-secure">Encrypted</span></div><p class=opsn-desc>Send a message directly on the membrane. IP hashed, never stored raw. For end-to-end encryption, use the external email option below.<form autocomplete=off class=opsn-form id=opsn-msg-form><input name=page type=hidden value=/analysis/how-to-build-an-os/><input name=tag type=hidden value=message><div class=opsn-field><label for=opsn-msg-body>Your message</label><textarea placeholder="What do you want to say? Be direct." id=opsn-msg-body maxlength=2000 minlength=10 name=body required rows=3></textarea></div><div class=opsn-field><label for=opsn-msg-contact>Contact (optional)</label><input placeholder="ProtonMail, Signal number, or leave blank" id=opsn-msg-contact maxlength=200 name=contact><span class=opsn-hint>Only used if we need to respond. Never published.</span></div><button class=opsn-submit id=opsn-msg-submit><span class=opsn-submit-text>Send Message</span> <span class=opsn-submit-sending style=display:none>Sending…</span></button><div class=opsn-result id=opsn-msg-result style=display:none></div></form><div style="border-top:1px solid #ffffff0d;margin-top:12px;padding-top:10px" class=opsn-email-actions><span style=color:#484f58;margin-right:8px;font-size:.8em>↗ prefer external email?</span><a href="mailto:eco.primal@pm.me?subject=Signal%3A%20How%20To%20Build%20an%20OS%20%E2%80%94%20Dykema%20Gossett%20and%20the%20Dark%20Money%20Machine%20%E2%80%94%20/analysis/how-to-build-an-os/&body=Page%3A%20https%3A//tuebor.primals.eco/analysis/how-to-build-an-os/%0A%0AObservation%3A%0A%0A" class=opsn-email-btn rel=noopener style=font-size:.85em> ProtonMail </a><a class="opsn-email-btn opsn-email-alt" href="mailto:hello@clutchjustice.com?subject=Re%3A%20How%20To%20Build%20an%20OS%20%E2%80%94%20Dykema%20Gossett%20and%20the%20Dark%20Money%20Machine&body=Page%3A%20https%3A//tuebor.primals.eco/analysis/how-to-build-an-os/%0A%0A" rel=noopener style=font-size:.85em> Clutch Justice </a></div><p class=opsn-tip>💡 <strong>Tip:</strong> If you are a government employee or officer of the court, consider using a personal email account for sensitive disclosures.</div></div><div class=opsn-feed id=opsn-feed style=display:none><h3>🧬 Network Signals</h3><p class=opsn-desc>Verified observations from the community.<div id=opsn-feed-list></div></div></section><script>(function() {
  var form = document.getElementById('opsn-form');
  var result = document.getElementById('opsn-result');
  var submitBtn = document.getElementById('opsn-submit');
  var submitText = submitBtn.querySelector('.opsn-submit-text');
  var submitSending = submitBtn.querySelector('.opsn-submit-sending');

  form.addEventListener('submit', function(e) {
    e.preventDefault();
    submitText.style.display = 'none';
    submitSending.style.display = 'inline';
    submitBtn.disabled = true;
    result.style.display = 'none';

    var fd = new FormData(form);
    var body = {};
    fd.forEach(function(v, k) { body[k] = v; });

    fetch('/api/opsonize', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify(body)
    })
    .then(function(r) { return r.json().then(function(d) { return {status: r.status, data: d}; }); })
    .then(function(res) {
      result.style.display = 'block';
      if (res.data.ok) {
        result.className = 'opsn-result opsn-result-ok';
        result.innerHTML = '<strong>✓ ' + escHtml(res.data.message) + '</strong><br>' +
          '<span class="opsn-tag-label">' + escHtml(res.data.tag) + '</span>: ' +
          escHtml(res.data.tag_meaning);
        form.reset();
      } else {
        result.className = 'opsn-result opsn-result-err';
        result.textContent = res.data.error + (res.data.detail ? ' — ' + res.data.detail : '');
      }
    })
    .catch(function(err) {
      result.style.display = 'block';
      result.className = 'opsn-result opsn-result-err';
      result.textContent = 'Network error — try the email channel instead.';
    })
    .finally(function() {
      submitText.style.display = 'inline';
      submitSending.style.display = 'none';
      submitBtn.disabled = false;
    });
  });

  // Load approved signals feed
  fetch('/api/opsonize/feed')
    .then(function(r) { return r.json(); })
    .then(function(data) {
      if (data.signals && data.signals.length > 0) {
        var feed = document.getElementById('opsn-feed');
        var list = document.getElementById('opsn-feed-list');
        var currentPage = form.querySelector('[name=page]').value;
        var relevant = data.signals.filter(function(s) { return s.page === currentPage; });
        if (relevant.length > 0) {
          feed.style.display = 'block';
          list.innerHTML = relevant.map(function(s) {
            return '<div class="opsn-signal-card">' +
              '<span class="opsn-tag-label">' + escHtml(s.tag) + '</span> ' +
              '<span class="opsn-signal-time">' + escHtml(s.ts.split('T')[0]) + '</span>' +
              '<p>' + escHtml(s.body) + '</p>' +
              '</div>';
          }).join('');
        }
      }
    })
    .catch(function() {});

  function escHtml(s) {
    var d = document.createElement('div');
    d.textContent = s || '';
    return d.innerHTML;
  }
})();</script><script src="/sensesjs/membrane-discuss.js?v=1" defer></script><script>// ── Message form handler (replaces mailto: popout) ──
(function() {
  var form = document.getElementById("opsn-msg-form");
  if (!form) return;
  var result = document.getElementById("opsn-msg-result");
  var btn = document.getElementById("opsn-msg-submit");
  var sendText = btn ? btn.querySelector(".opsn-submit-text") : null;
  var sendSending = btn ? btn.querySelector(".opsn-submit-sending") : null;

  form.addEventListener("submit", function(e) {
    e.preventDefault();
    if (sendText) sendText.style.display = "none";
    if (sendSending) sendSending.style.display = "inline";
    if (btn) btn.disabled = true;
    if (result) result.style.display = "none";

    var fd = new FormData(form);
    var data = {};
    fd.forEach(function(v, k) { data[k] = v; });

    fetch("/api/opsonize", {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      body: JSON.stringify(data)
    })
    .then(function(r) { return r.json().then(function(d) { return { status: r.status, data: d }; }); })
    .then(function(res) {
      if (result) result.style.display = "block";
      if (res.data.ok) {
        if (result) {
          result.className = "opsn-result opsn-result-ok";
          result.innerHTML = "<strong>Message sent.</strong> Delivered on the membrane.";
        }
        form.reset();
      } else {
        if (result) {
          result.className = "opsn-result opsn-result-err";
          result.textContent = res.data.error || "Error sending message";
        }
      }
    })
    .catch(function() {
      if (result) {
        result.style.display = "block";
        result.className = "opsn-result opsn-result-err";
        result.textContent = "Network error. Try the external email option.";
      }
    })
    .finally(function() {
      if (sendText) sendText.style.display = "inline";
      if (sendSending) sendSending.style.display = "none";
      if (btn) btn.disabled = false;
