    </script><body><a class=skip-link href=#main>Skip to content</a><nav class=site-nav><div class=nav-inner><a class=nav-brand href=/tuebor>tuebor</a><div class=nav-links><a href=/tuebor style=color:khaki;font-weight:700>🔍 Explore</a><a href=/tueboractors/>Actors</a><a href=/tueborevidence/>Evidence</a><a href=/tueboranalysis/>Analysis</a><a href=/tueborinvestigate/>Investigate</a><a href=/tuebortimeline/>Timeline</a><a href=/tueborsynthesis/ style=color:#98fb98>Dialectic</a><a href=/tuebor-desk style=opacity:.7;font-size:.85em>⊞ Desk</a><a href=/tuebormembrane/ style=opacity:.7;font-size:.85em>⬡ Membrane</a><a href=/map style=opacity:.7;font-size:.85em>🗺️ Map</a></div><div class=nav-search><input aria-label="Search articles" placeholder="Search Beasley, Moran, PCA..." autocomplete=off id=tuebor-search><div class=search-results id=tuebor-search-results style=display:none></div></div></div></nav><main class=site-main id=main><article class="page-content home-content"><h2 id=tuebor-i-will-defend>Tuebor — “I Will Defend”</h2><p>It is the motto on Michigan’s state seal.<p>It is what happens when citizens discover that the institutions designed to protect them have stopped working — and decide to document the failure themselves.<hr><h2 id=rotating-light-october-16-2026-ex-parte-ppo-filed-against-this-project>🚨 October 16, 2026: Ex Parte PPO Filed Against This Project</h2><p><strong>Brian Roderick Banks</strong> — a convicted felon and subject of this investigation — filed an <strong>ex parte Personal Protection Order</strong> against the operator of this infrastructure on the same day he was attending a meeting. An ex parte order is obtained without the target being present — one side tells their story to a judge in secret.<p>This is the pattern: publish verifiable public records → receive legal retaliation. First a <a href=/evidence/slapp-timeline/>SLAPP suit</a> (November 2025). Now an ex parte PPO (October 2026). The legal weapons escalate each time the published record expands.<p><strong><a href=/evidence/slapp-timeline/>Read the complete SLAPP timeline →</a></strong><p>The record remains. Every fact is cited. Every document is timestamped. The infrastructure is sovereign.<hr><h2 id=red-circle-new-following-the-money-through-the-blind-spots>🔴 New: Following the Money Through the Blind Spots</h2><p><strong><a href=/analysis/the-nulls-that-point/>The Nulls That Point</a></strong> — 73 entities in the investigation graph had no classification. We backtracked them. They formed three hidden networks: a PAC formation machine, a media pipeline, and a constellation of LLCs — all operating in the blind spots between regulators. The unknowns pointed to the knowns.<p><strong><a href=/analysis/the-architect-and-the-clerk/>The Architect and the Clerk</a></strong> — One Dykema attorney (Wilk) drafted Michigan’s charter school law. Then formed 10+ PACs protecting it. One compliance specialist (Moore) governs 6 PACs, employed simultaneously by Banks AND PCA AND Dykema. The architecture is not accidental. It was designed.<p><strong><a href=/evidence/the-money-flows-through-nulls/>The Money Flows Through Nulls</a></strong> — Walton → Martin → Banks in 3 hops. Money enters as foundation funding. It exits as narrative cover. The SCBC Tour is funded by Walton, produced by NuVision, partnered with AFC/EdChoice/ExcelinEd. Follow the money through the entities nobody classified.<hr><h2 id=red-circle-the-regulator-problem>🔴 The Regulator Problem</h2><p><strong><a href=/analysis/the-call-is-coming-from-inside-the-fcc/>The Call Is Coming from Inside the FCC</a></strong> — You get spam calls. The FCC knows who sends them. Every voice service provider must register, file a Robocall Mitigation Plan, and comply with STIR/SHAKEN. The FCC has the database. The Industry Traceback Group traces every robocall to its origin carrier. They know. They have always known. Same architecture as MDE sitting above Banks. Same silence.<p><strong><a href=/analysis/the-regulator-who-regulates-the-regulator/>The Regulator Who Regulates the Regulator</a></strong> — MDE/CMU/PCA, FCC/VoIP/CallCenter, AGC/StateBar/Courts — three different regulatory ecosystems, same 5-layer template, same blind spot. Each regulator’s budget depends on the regulated industry’s size. TCPA exists because Congress knew the FCC wouldn’t act.<p><strong><a href=/evidence/fcc-enforcement-pattern/>FCC Enforcement by the Numbers</a></strong> — $2B+ proposed fines. Less than 2% collected. 0.5% enforcement rate. STIR/SHAKEN exemptions for the exact small VoIP providers sending the spam. The pattern is identical to Michigan charter school oversight.<hr><h2 id=red-circle-banks-investigation-convictions-2-charter-schools>🔴 Banks Investigation — 9 Convictions, 2 Charter Schools</h2><p><strong><a href=/analysis/they-banked-on-banks/>They Banked on Banks</a></strong> — Brian Roderick Banks has 9 criminal convictions and runs Purpose Charter Academy and MacDowell Preparatory Academy in Detroit. His board chair is a sitting Wayne County judge. His receptionist blocks parents at the door. His PPO motion blocks them in court. 362 students. 99.2% Black. 3% math proficiency. 72.67% revenue extracted by a single-member LLC.<p><strong><a href=/analysis/signal-permeability/>Signal Permeability</a></strong> — Live experiment: we sent the evidence to every oversight body. Now we’re measuring who opens it. First confirmed reader: <strong>Lansing, Michigan</strong> — the state capital. <a href=/analysis/signal-permeability/>Read the live data →</a><hr><h2 id=red-circle-the-infrastructure>🔴 The Infrastructure</h2><p><strong><a href=/evidence/every-tower-every-wire-every-orbit/>Every Tower, Every Wire, Every Orbit</a></strong> — 134 Detroit antenna structures.<p><strong><a href=/evidence/every-line-every-peak-every-depth/>Every Line, Every Peak, Every Depth</a></strong> — The complete topology of Earth. 50 states, 109 borders, 63 national parks, every high point from Denali (20,310 ft) to Britton Hill (345 ft). The Grand Canyon: 278 miles, 2 billion years of rock, a 1.2 billion year gap. 16 tectonic plates. Challenger Deep at 36,201 feet below sea level. The ground we stand on. CMU Public Broadcasting owns 11 towers across Michigan (including a 1,177-ft tower in Atlanta, MI). 11,156 Starlink satellites. 2 Michigan ground stations. 535 miles of new submarine fiber crossing Lake Michigan. The physical infrastructure map of who controls the signals.<p><strong><a href=/analysis/can-the-membrane-filter-your-phone/>Can the Membrane Filter Your Phone?</a></strong> — Honest analysis: STIR/SHAKEN is the phone network’s immune system. It’s broken because exemptions exist for small VoIP providers — the exact ones sending spam. The architecture is identical to web security. The world gets quieter when the membrane has no exemptions.<hr><h2 id=the-dialectic-the-investigation-questions-itself>The Dialectic — The Investigation Questions Itself</h2><p><strong><a href=/synthesis/what-if-we-are-the-pattern/>Antithesis — What If We Are the Pattern?</a></strong> — The strongest version of the counterargument. What if the investigation is pareidolia? What if null is the answer? What if the membrane is a cage? Every investigation owes itself the sharpest knife it can find.<p><strong><a href=/synthesis/the-soft-the-hard-the-still/>Synthesis — The Soft, the Hard, and the Still</a></strong> — 341 entities classified. 60 bedrock, 136 hardening, 114 boundary, 70 soft, 100 still, 103 borrowed. What we know, what we don’t, and where we’re borrowing certainty.<p><strong><a href=/synthesis/the-things-that-follow/>Corollary — The Things That Follow</a></strong> — If the thesis is true, what else must be true? If the antithesis is true, what else must be true? The logic goes where it goes whether we steer it or not.<hr><h2 id=for-researchers-journalists-advocates>For Researchers, Journalists, Advocates</h2><p><strong><a href=/analysis/the-ones-who-showed-up/>The Ones Who Showed Up</a></strong> — Dr. Beasley. Dr. Lenhoff at Wayne State PEER. Carol Burris at NPE. Diane Ravitch. Skillman Foundation. Misha Stallworth West. Ahmed Beasley. ACLU Michigan. CitizenDetroit. Rita at Clutch Justice. They did the work. We built the cross-links. Point back.<p><strong><a href=/investigate/how-to-point-back/>How to Point Back</a></strong> — Stable URLs, key pages to cite, how cross-links work, what each audience can contribute. Legal paths: TCPA, PA 362, qui tam, IRS whistleblower, § 1983.<p><strong><a href=/investigate/spam-call-traceback/>How to Trace a Spam Call</a></strong> — Step-by-step: document the call, look up the carrier, check the FCC databases, file complaints, enable protections, sue under TCPA ($500–$1,500 per illegal call, private right of action).<hr><h2 id=why-this-site-exists>Why This Site Exists</h2><p>Michigan’s oversight systems are failing across counties.<p>The <strong>Attorney Grievance Commission</strong> dismisses 94% of complaints. The <strong>Judicial Tenure Commission</strong> operates on timelines measured in years. The <strong>State Court Administrative Office</strong> receives documented structural failures and responds with silence. Courts ignore evidence placed before them on their own dockets.<p>These are not isolated failures. They are the same system, producing the same outcomes, in every county:<table><thead><tr><th>County<th>What Failed<th>Status<tbody><tr><td><strong>Wayne (Detroit)</strong><td>A convicted felon runs charter schools with a sitting judge and assistant attorney general on his board. AGC and JTC notified.<td><a href=/detroit rel=external>Evidence published →</a><tr><td><strong>Saginaw</strong><td>An attorney submitted a witness who does not exist. The court signed a contempt order against the journalist who documented it.<td><a href=/evidence/ghost-witness-aljouny/>Evidence below ↓</a><tr><td><strong>Barry</strong><td>A judge disappeared from the bench. The court said nothing. SCAO was filed on. The feds stepped in.<td>Tracking<tr><td><strong>Macomb</strong><td>A manufactured PPO violation tied to a Facebook account the target never owned.<td>Tracking<tr><td><strong>Allegan</strong><td>A deputy ran the wrong plate, shot a 22-year-old. Four years later, the record doesn’t add up.<td>Tracking<tr><td><strong>Eastpointe (38th District)</strong><td>A judge jailed a pregnant woman over fines, listed dead attorneys as endorsers, and received a confidential JTC admonition.<td>Tracking</table><p>The pattern is not partisan. It is not geographic. It is structural.<p>When oversight stops working, the only defense left is the record itself.<hr><h2 id=the-connective-tissue>The Connective Tissue</h2><p>These are not separate problems. They share the same root:<p><strong>The AGC that dismisses 94% of complaints</strong> is the same AGC that received documented evidence of an assistant attorney general sitting on a convicted felon’s charter school board — and has not acted.<p><strong>The SCAO that took years to address Barry County</strong> is the same SCAO that was notified that a sitting 3rd Circuit judge serves as president of a charter school board alongside that same convicted felon — and has not acted.<p><strong>The court in Saginaw that ignored a fabricated witness</strong> is the same judicial system where a court in Wayne County processes custody matters that send children to schools run by people with 9 criminal convictions.<p>When one node fails, the others should catch it. They don’t. The system does not self-correct. So citizens correct the record.<hr><h2 id=evidence>Evidence</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Investigation<th>Source<th>Status<tbody><tr><td><strong><a href=/evidence/ghost-witness-aljouny/>Ghost Witness — Samantha Aljouny</a></strong><td>Court records, ProtonMail forensics, controlled link test, independent journalist confirmation<td>IC3 complaint filed Oct 6, 2026. 13 convergence points.<tr><td><strong><a href=/evidence/data-braid-aljouny/>Data Braid — Public vs. Private Evidence</a></strong><td>ARIN WHOIS, MPSC registry, OLC press archive, LARA, PACER, Times Herald, SCOTUS records<td>6 reverse target searches. All independently confirmed from public sources.<tr><td><strong><a href=/evidence/domain-registrations/>Domain Registration Campaign</a></strong><td>WHOIS, GoDaddy records, PPO filings, Clutch Justice reporting<td>3 domains targeting PPO holders (incl. minor child) registered in 30 min. Renewed Sep 2026. Impersonation site live.<tr><td><strong><a href=/evidence/foiaworks-honeypot/>FOIAworks Honeypot Analysis</a></strong><td>LARA entity search, FOIAworks ToS, 404 at /privacy/, Quagmire Solutions LLC<td>Fabricated-witness attorney operates FOIA platform with no privacy policy.<tr><td><strong><a href=/evidence/foiaworks-early-warning/>FOIAworks as Early Warning System</a></strong><td>8+ FOIA lawsuits, county relationship map, Higgins Lake connection, Statewide plan intelligence risk<td>The attorney who sued FOIA coordinators across Michigan now operates the platform investigators file through.<tr><td><strong><a href=/evidence/ellison-sanctions/>$74,752.45: Federal Sanctions</a></strong><td>PACER (W.D. Mich., 6th Cir. 22-1574), SCOTUS No. 23-404, E.D. Mich. 21-cv-12250<td>Two courts: $73K (6th Cir.) + $1K (E.D. Mich.). SCOTUS cert denied.<tr><td><strong><a href=/evidence/litigation-docket/>Complete Litigation Docket</a></strong><td>PACER, PacerMonitor, Leagle, COA 374178, OLC press releases<td>Every active and resolved case. Wins, reversals, sanctions, docket patterns. OLC v. Treasury FOIA dismissed for notary failure.<tr><td><strong><a href=/evidence/impersonation-domain/>Impersonation Domain</a></strong><td>WHOIS, court transcript Aug 3, 2026, NCMEC CyberTip 222110727<td>ritafelinewilliams.com — live, collecting data, renewed Sep 2026. Attorney stated on record client “created the domains.”<tr><td><strong><a href=/evidence/the-money-flows-through-nulls/>The Money Flows Through Nulls</a></strong><td>IRS 990, TransparencyUSA, LARA, campaign finance, Foundation Center<td>Walton→Martin→Banks: 3 hops. SCBC Tour convergence. NuVision→50CAN→The 74 pipeline.<tr><td><strong><a href=/evidence/fcc-enforcement-pattern/>FCC Enforcement Pattern</a></strong><td>FCC Enforcement Bureau, Robocall Mitigation Database, STIR/SHAKEN data<td>$2B+ proposed fines, &lt;2% collected, 0.5% enforcement. Same pattern as charter school oversight.<tr><td><strong><a href=/evidence/every-tower-every-wire-every-orbit/>Every Tower, Every Wire, Every Orbit</a></strong><td>FCC ASR, CelesTrak, NTIA IMPACC, Peninsula Fiber Network filings<td>134 Detroit towers, 11 CMU towers, 11,156 Starlink satellites, 535 miles submarine fiber.</table><hr><h2 id=documented-actors>Documented Actors</h2><p>Sourced profiles of every actor in the investigation. Every role documented to court records or public filings.<table><thead><tr><th>Actor<th>Role<th>Investigation<tbody><tr><td><strong><a href=/actors/ellison/>Philip L. Ellison</a></strong><td>Attorney, 4 entities, 153-domain portfolio, $74K federal sanctions, fabricated witness. SCOTUS win AND sanctions on same docket.<td>Aljouny / Saginaw<tr><td><strong><a href=/actors/lindke/>Kevin Lindke</a></strong><td>Ellison’s client. Convicted: computer crime. 272 days served. 21K-member Facebook group. Domains in minor child’s name.<td>Aljouny / Saginaw<tr><td><strong><a href=/actors/gafkay/>Judge Julie A. Gafkay</a></strong><td>Chief Judge, 10th Circuit. SVSU colleague of Ellison. 3 simultaneous Ellison cases.<td>Aljouny / Saginaw<tr><td><strong><a href=/actors/borrello/>Judge Andre R. Borrello</a></strong><td>Signed contempt, then recused himself.<td>Aljouny / Saginaw<tr><td><strong><a href=/actors/ellsworth/>Kelly D. Ellsworth</a></strong><td>Briefly represented Rita. Dissuaded her. SCBA insider, family in bar since 1986.<td>Structural / Saginaw<tr><td><strong><a href=/actors/galen/>Judge Kathleen G. Galen</a></strong><td>JTC admonition. Jailed pregnant woman (reversed). Campaign staff = court staff.<td>Eastpointe / 38th District<tr><td><strong><a href=/actors/schipper/>Judge Michael Schipper</a></strong><td>Active JTC investigation. 6–10x guideline sentencing. ADA retaliation.<td>Barry County<tr><td><strong><a href=/actors/nakfoor-pratt/>Julie Nakfoor Pratt</a></strong><td>Private admonishment (MRPC 3.4(e)). Brady/Giglio failures. FOIA obstruction.<td>Barry County</table><p>Full actor index: <strong><a href=/actors/>All Actors →</a></strong><hr><h2 id=investigation-toolkit><a href=/investigate/>Investigation Toolkit</a></h2><p>Everything you need to run your own Michigan accountability investigation:<table><thead><tr><th>Tool<th>What It Does<tbody><tr><td><strong><a href=/investigate/foia-toolkit/>FOIA Toolkit</a></strong><td>Templates, deadlines, exemption challenges, appeal paths<tr><td><strong><a href=/investigate/hemlock-foia/>Hemlock FOIA Toolkit</a></strong><td>Ready-to-use templates: Saginaw ISD contracts, Hemlock PS “Humans of Hemlock”, LakeNet vendor records, Roscommon property deed<tr><td><strong><a href=/investigate/oversight-guide/>Oversight Filing Guide</a></strong><td>How to file with AGC, JTC, SCAO, MCOLES, IC3<tr><td><strong><a href=/investigate/court-records/>Court Records Guide</a></strong><td>Dockets, appellate opinions, PACER, LARA, campaign finance<tr><td><strong><a href=/investigate/evidence-documentation/>Evidence Documentation</a></strong><td>Incident logs, document indexes, preservation notices<tr><td><strong><a href=/investigate/spam-call-traceback/>How to Trace a Spam Call</a></strong><td>Document → lookup carrier → check FCC databases → file complaints → sue under TCPA<tr><td><strong><a href=/investigate/how-to-point-back/>How to Point Back</a></strong><td>Stable URLs, key pages to cite, legal paths. For researchers, journalists, advocates, parents, lawyers.</table><hr><h2 id=timeline><a href=/timeline/>Timeline</a></h2><p>Chronological record from 2013 to present. Every entry sourced.<hr><h2 id=analysis><a href=/analysis/>Analysis</a></h2><h3 id=infrastructure-studies-how-the-systems-work>Infrastructure Studies — How the Systems Work</h3><ul><li><strong><a href=/analysis/sitting-in-a-tree/>Sitting in a Tree</a></strong> — Mike and Tom and Dykema and Banks, K-I-S-S-I-N-G. One law firm, one compliance specialist, four branches. Same donors, same dark money, same day. First comes money, then comes power, then comes a charter school with convicted felons in the tower. The trilogy completes.<li><strong><a href=/analysis/hey-mikey/>Hey Mikey, He Likes It!</a></strong> — Rogers authored America’s most aggressive surveillance bill (killed twice), got hired by the company whose competitor he investigated, bought a $1.6M house in Florida, and accepted $88.8M from Texas oil, Blackstone, Citadel, Koch, McConnell, and Musk. Same donors fund Barrett. Same Dykema OS. Same election. He’ll eat anything.<li><strong><a href=/analysis/enforcement-ecosystem/>The Enforcement Ecosystem</a></strong> — Ten oversight bodies have the mandate, the evidence, and the authority. None has the full picture. State Bar closed the UPL file. AGC sent it back. Two letters, one day apart, each pointing at the other door. The network operates in the jurisdictional gaps between them.<li><strong><a href=/analysis/tommy-boy/>Tommy Boy</a></strong> — Barrett calls his opponent a “convicted felon” (expunged). Barrett’s PAC donor runs dark money with an actual convicted felon as president. FEC receipts. Nov 3, 2026.<li><strong><a href=/analysis/how-to-build-an-os/>How To Build an OS</a></strong> — One law firm (Dykema), one compliance specialist (Moore), 7+ dark money vehicles, both parties served. SDJ’s phone number is Dykema’s phone number. All public records.<li><strong><a href=/analysis/infrastructure-grid/>Infrastructure Grid</a></strong> — Fluorescent tag map: every node where entity infrastructure touches individual privacy. 11 nodes. FOIAworks has no privacy policy. SDJ hides donors. Domains By Proxy hides websites. The protections point the wrong direction.<li><strong><a href=/analysis/lakenet-signal-trace/>LakeNet Signal Trace</a></strong> — One IP, three captures, one ISP in a town of 1,500. The tracer isotope that illuminates every connection sharing the infrastructure.<li><strong><a href=/analysis/anderson-hemlock/>Anderson Localization — Hemlock</a></strong> — Same physics as Detroit, population 2,000, one family captures every layer</ul><h3 id=pattern-analysis-how-oversight-fails>Pattern Analysis — How Oversight Fails</h3><ul><li><strong><a href=/analysis/cross-subgraph-patterns/>Cross-Subgraph Patterns</a></strong> — How Detroit, Saginaw, Barry, Macomb, and Allegan connect through the same AGC, JTC, SCAO, and LARA nodes<li><strong><a href=/analysis/upepa-contradiction/>The UPEPA Contradiction</a></strong> — Michigan’s anti-SLAPP statute weaponized by its first stress-tester<li><strong><a href=/analysis/institutional-immunity/>Institutional Immunity</a></strong> — AGC dismisses 88.8% of complaints (their own data)<li><strong><a href=/analysis/credential-vs-conduct/>Credential vs. Conduct</a></strong> — The resume says SCOTUS champion. The docket says sanctioned, reversed, SLAPP-filing, representing a convicted harasser.</ul><h3 id=new-dark-money-networks-and-regulatory-capture>New: Dark Money Networks and Regulatory Capture</h3><ul><li><strong><a href=/analysis/the-nulls-that-point/>The Nulls That Point</a></strong> — 73 unclassified entities, 3 hidden networks discovered by backtracking through the blind spots<li><strong><a href=/analysis/the-architect-and-the-clerk/>The Architect and the Clerk</a></strong> — Wilk drafted PA 362, then formed 10+ PACs protecting it. Moore governs 6 PACs across both parties simultaneously.<li><strong><a href=/analysis/the-call-is-coming-from-inside-the-fcc/>The Call Is Coming from Inside the FCC</a></strong> — The FCC knows who sends your spam calls. Same regulatory architecture as MDE. Same silence.<li><strong><a href=/analysis/the-regulator-who-regulates-the-regulator/>The Regulator Who Regulates the Regulator</a></strong> — Three ecosystems, one template, one blind spot<li><strong><a href=/analysis/can-the-membrane-filter-your-phone/>Can the Membrane Filter Your Phone?</a></strong> — STIR/SHAKEN, broken exemptions, and why the world gets quieter when there are no holes<li><strong><a href=/analysis/the-ones-who-showed-up/>The Ones Who Showed Up</a></strong> — Credits and cross-links to every ally who did the work</ul><hr><h2 id=how-this-works>How This Works</h2><ul><li><strong>No cookies.</strong> No tracking. No identifying data.<li><strong>Every claim</strong> sourced to court records, public filings, or verifiable data.<li><strong>The git repository</strong> contains source material. Clone it. Verify it. Audit it.<li><strong>Cross-protection:</strong> Evidence published across multiple nodes in the <a href=/ rel=external>primals.eco</a> network cannot be suppressed by silencing any single person. SLAPP one — the others amplify.<li><strong>209 articles.</strong> 210,000+ words. 7,533 investigation nodes. 131,322 edges. All public record.</ul><hr><h2 id=who-we-are>Who We Are</h2><p>People who read court records, file FOIA requests, attend hearings, submit amicus briefs, make AGC and JTC complaints, and publish what we find.<p>We are not attorneys. We are not parties to each other’s cases. We are citizens exercising First Amendment rights to document institutional accountability — or its absence.<p>Some of us are investigative journalists. Some are parents. Some are both.<p>Michigan’s seal says <em>tuebor</em>. We are taking it literally.<hr><p><em>This site is part of the <a href=/ rel=external>primals.eco</a> evidence network.</em> <em>Detroit node: <a href=/detroit rel=external>detroit.primals.eco</a></em> <em>115 pages. Every claim sourced. Come and see.</em></article></main><footer class=site-footer><p><strong>Every fact is cited. Every document is timestamped.</strong><p>Source: <a href=http://nestgate.io:3000/publicRecord/detroit>git repository</a> — clone it, verify it. <br>No cookies. No tracking. No identifying data.<p>Part of the <a href=/>primals.eco</a> evidence network: <a href=/detroit>detroit</a> · <a href=/tuebor>lansing</a> · <a href=/signal>signal</a> · <a href=/dialectic>hypothesis</a> · <a href=/senses>hud</a> · <a href=/record>clutch</a><p class=footer-license>Original analysis: <a href=https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/>CC-BY-SA 4.0</a>. Court filings and public records: public domain where applicable.<p>Named on this site? Something wrong? <a onclick="var el=document.getElementById('opsonize');if(el){el.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'});return false}" href=#opsonize>Contact us</a> (<a href=mailto:eco.primal@pm.me style=opacity:.6;font-size:.85em>or email ↗</a>) — truth matters more than being right.<p style=margin-top:.5rem;font-size:.8rem><a href=https://github.com/amicusContra/tuebor style=opacity:.6>Source: github.com/amicusContra/tuebor</a> · <a href=/dialectic style=opacity:.6>sporePrint</a> · <a href=/dialectic style=opacity:.6>thesis</a> · <a href=/dialectic style=opacity:.6>hypothesis</a> · <a href=/dialectic style=opacity:.6>synthesis</a> · <a href=/dialectic style=opacity:.6>antithesis</a> · <a href=/dialectic style=opacity:.6>corollary</a> · <a href=/dialectic style=opacity:.6>totality</a></footer><script src=/tueborjs/elasticlunr.min.js></script><script src=/tueborsearch_index.en.js></script><script src=/tueborjs/search.js></script><script defer src=/sensesjs/hud-widget.js></script>
